## Review notes

During copy-completeness review, an initial mechanical removal accidentally removed `disposeModelStack()` and `initModel()` along with the moved context/session block. This was corrected before syntax and smoke testing. The final staged `llama_worker/llama.mjs` preserves both functions inline; lifecycle extraction remains out of scope.

## Caveats / known risks

```text
Finding:
  Context retry/session service extraction moves code that coordinates context creation aborts, partial artifact cleanup, session insertion, and resetSession waits.
Affected surface:
  createSessionContextWithRetry, getSession, resetSession, contextController ownership, active session eviction.
Why it matters:
  Small ordering drift could cause canceled context creation to retry, partial artifacts to leak, active sessions to be evicted, or resetSession to dispose before request boundaries settle.
Smallest safe correction:
  Keep contextController ownership in the context retry service, keep session insertion after successful wrapper creation, and keep resetSession ordering as abort -> wait boundaries -> dispose.
What still needs verification:
  Michael real-runtime context/session carry-forward gates before merge readiness.
```

